From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan <ryan@esterlines.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:44:37 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb+LibWebView+WebContent: Add an element picker for
 cosmetic filters

uBlock Origin's element picker lets the user click something on a page
and hide it from then on. ViewImplementation::start_element_picker()
does the same with the node picker DevTools uses: it highlights what is
under the pointer, and on a click asks WebContent for a cosmetic filter
that hides the picked element on its site. The filter uses the element's
id, or its tag and classes, when they pick out only it, and otherwise
the shortest path of child combinators (from the nearest ancestor with
an id) that does. A text node stands for the element holding it.

A frontend starts it, from its context menu for instance, and can show
the resulting filter for the user to confirm or edit. Settings::
add_custom_content_blocker_filter() then adds it to the custom filters,
which applies it to every page at once.

Internals exposes the filter generator for tests.
